Scope:

This LICENSE (CC BY-NC 4.0) applies to DOCUMENTATION in this repository:
walkthroughs (WRITEUPS/01 Hack The Box/), security reference categories
(APPLICATIONS/, INFRASTRUCTURE/, AI/, NETWORKS/, ANONYMITY-PRIVACY-OPSEC/,
CLOUD/, VIRTUALIZATION/, INFORMATION_SECURITY/, OSINT/), methodology/OSCP-Reporting.md,
METHODOLOGY.md, CHEATSHEET.md, README.md, SECURITY.md, and other
prose/Markdown content across root, tools/, site/, and app/.

SOURCE CODE AND INFRASTRUCTURE definitions are licensed separately under the MIT License.
The MIT license applies to all executable source files, web components,
and infrastructure configurations in this repository, including:

  - tools/**/*.py, tools/**/*.go, tools/**/*.sh         (see tools/LICENSE)
  - site/src/**, site/scripts/**, site/*.js              (Docusaurus portal & Lenses Hub)
  - app/bff/**, app/frontend/**, app/security-monitor/** (Workers, API, SPA)
  - terraform/**/*.tf, terraform/**/*.tfvars.example     (Cloudflare Pages IaC)
  - check.ps1, mask.ps1, audit.ps1, check-anchors.ps1,
    check-tables.ps1, audit-session.ps1, writeup-spec.psd1,
    tests/run-tests.ps1                                  (automation & verification scripts)

If a file is ambiguous, the following rule applies:
  - .md, .txt, .rst                                      -> CC BY-NC 4.0 (this license)
  - .py, .go, .sh, .ps1, .psd1                           -> MIT
  - .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .css, .tf, .toml               -> MIT
  - .yml (GitHub Actions workflows)                      -> MIT

Note: the rule above is file-type based. Markdown documentation inside
tools/, site/, or app/ (e.g. tools/python/README.md, site/README.md,
app/frontend/README.md) is CC BY-NC 4.0 like all other .md files in this
repository, even though the source code in the same directories is MIT.
tools/LICENSE contains the MIT text that applies to source code across the repository.

